{"skill":{"slug":"pdf-generator","displayName":"Pdf Generator"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1771465920711,"changelog":"Improved security documentation and scope clarity","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"EXTRA_FILES.txt","size":34,"sha256":"260ac286d4388b799179386b1a6a39d20dcf190f3d147d1b80fe06e128333d89","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3378,"sha256":"e9837714a868dbafe7c9816c7b4afd2ce5a1ca34f5e1683fb46b6e235c1f85c1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"advanced.md","size":4637,"sha256":"36c1000ef6e6b5f3c288ca139359d68f517dcc7a6f4f5c4b768382c69cd69790","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"templates.md","size":9117,"sha256":"4854cd970b59ef51151d3713ab9330ae88e1cbd50bd43f26ed092876150cefc7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tools.md","size":2332,"sha256":"dadfd3007d33581dfb562b822be5c1a0efdd58a77936da0dddf1c7a5fbba3b35","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2306,"sha256":"244fadd2480b50e89dc0c3805a2db392dcb9184e3fc0f8c215a4ceff07993564","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789073362346,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"5a8b12ad70dc5068404515bea4f46e3c2fa9aa675b77e5d7a299b728c87b8a50","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/5a8b12ad70dc5068404515bea4f46e3c2fa9aa675b77e5d7a299b728c87b8a50","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: pdf-generator\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle provides documentation and code examples for local PDF generation using standard Python libraries (pypdf, weasyprint, reportlab, fpdf2) and suggests external tools like pandoc. The SKILL.md explicitly states that the skill 'NEVER executes code or generates files directly,' 'NEVER makes network requests,' and 'NEVER accesses files outside user's working directory.' The code examples align with these constraints, performing only local file operations for PDF creation. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, unauthorized command execution, persistence mechanisms, or prompt injection attempts against the agent. All operations are confined to the stated purpose of generating PDFs.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779165336383},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":7,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789073362346},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a documentation-only PDF generation skill with expected local file-output examples, but users should treat the sample paths and HTML templating as unsafe for untrusted input without hardening.","dimensions":[{"detail":"PDF generation naturally involves local reads and writes, and the package does not request runtime authority itself; copied examples using arbitrary paths or WeasyPrint should be constrained by the user.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No executable scripts, install hooks, dependency manifests, or hidden setup behavior were found; metadata only declares markdown skill content.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The main skill says it does not execute code or create files directly, which matches the markdown-only package, but examples should more clearly warn about overwrites, path confinement, and escaping untrusted template data.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, background workers, memory modification, credential handling, privilege escalation, or tool hijacking instructions were found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill coherently provides PDF generation guidance, tool selection, templates, and advanced PDF operations; the observed file writes are example outputs that fit the stated purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Safe to install as reference material. Before using the snippets in real applications, write outputs only to chosen directories, avoid overwriting important files, sanitize filenames, escape or template untrusted HTML data, and restrict WeasyPrint resource fetching if inputs can come from other users.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The missing side-effect warnings are valid documentation-quality concerns because examples create or modify PDFs, but this is expected for a PDF generator and not hidden runtime behavior.\n[T09] unexpected: The static path and HTML-injection concerns are credible if users adapt the examples for untrusted input; they affect sample-code robustness rather than showing malicious or automatically executed skill behavior.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789073362346}}}}}